<title>HONG KONG: Gold closes firmer in Hong Kong, trade quiet.</title>
<headline>Gold closes firmer in Hong Kong, trade quiet.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong gold ended firmer on Friday in light two-way trading following modest overnight gains, dealers said.</p>
<p>Bullion ended at US$369.10/60 an ounce against New York's US$368.60/369.10 close on Thursday.</p>
<p>Dealers said they expected bullion to move narrowly with most players quiet after Christmas and before New Year holidays.</p>
<p>Local gold ended at HK$3,410 a tael, up slightly from its previous close of HK$3,408 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The carryover charge at the Chinese Gold and Silver Exchange Society fell to -5.00 from its previous fix at -3.00.</p>
<p>BULLION -</p>
<p>Hong Kong close  - US$369.10/369.60</p>
<p>Hong Kong midday - US$369.00/369.50</p>
<p> Hong Kong open   - US$368.70/369.20</p>
<p> New York close   - US$368.60/369.10</p>
<p>HONG KONG TAEL MARKET -</p>
<p> Close		- HK$3,410</p>
<p> Midday	     - HK$3,410</p>
<p> Open		 - HK$3,409</p>
<p> Previous close   - HK$3,408</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
